GPT's second analysis is strong: **mechanism F — read-completion TOCTOU**. FIX1 guards at FUA-read *submit*; if the buffer was clean at submit but a transaction logs the split into it while the read is *in flight*, the read *completion* DMAs the stale/pristine disk image over `bp->b_addr` — and the submit-time guard never fires (clean at submit), exactly matching "P91-FUA-SKIP-LOGGED never fires on bnobt." The fix: bounce-buffer read + revalidate-after-I/O before copying.

